=begin pod

In the Raku community, there are a number of different projects/teams in which 
people participate.  In this article, I'll be calling these groups of people 
"Troupes".  Troupes are groups of people working together with a common purpose 
or purposes, and they usually have one or more projects in their troupe.  

As you become more involved in the Raku community, you will likely end up 
working with one of these Troupes; even if it's only a bug report, or a typo 
correction in the documentation, you will work with the appropriate troupe to 
resolve this.  

Each Troupe may also have a number of Hats that people wear. 

Some Troupes (such as the Modules Troupe) are divided into multiple Crews, which 
are the same concept, but at the next level down.  

The following are the current Troupes.  

=item The L<Modules|module/> Troupe works on the modules for Raku.  As a 
developer, this is one of the easiest to participate in.  

=item The L<Documentation|documentation/> Troupe works on the content of the 
documentation

=item The L<Web Framework|web-framework/> Troupe works on the frameworks that 
support the Raku websites, including raku.org and the documentation website.  

=item The L<Outreach|outreach/> Troupe works on making it easier for people to 
enter the community, and making it easier for people to share Raku with their 
associates.  

=item L<Rakudo|rakudo/> - These people work on the Rakudo compiler for Raku, and 
its underlying structures such as MoarVM, the virtual machine it runs on.  

=item The L<DevOps|devops/> Troupe works on making sure the underlying 
infrastructure for Raku keeps working.  

=end pod
